# Hearth's updater checks a download against the SHA256SUMS the author
# published, so every copy of a file has to be byte-for-byte identical
# everywhere. Git's default on Windows rewrites line endings on checkout,
# which changes the bytes and therefore the checksum: a maintainer who
# generated SHA256SUMS on a Windows checkout would publish digests that no
# download could ever match, and updates would fail for everyone.
#
# Pinning the endings keeps the working tree, the repository and the release
# zip in agreement on every platform. LF is what is already committed here,
# so nothing that ships changes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Not text - never touch these.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jar binary
*.zip binary
